      <li><strong>2022–2023:</strong> Annual additions exceeded 1,800 and 2,300 respectively, driven by Starlink Group launches and the onset of Amazon Kuiper deployments.</li>
      <li><strong>2024–2025:</strong> The curve steepened further. By end-2025, the catalog stood at {stats['cumulative_2025']:,} active satellites — a {stats['cumulative_2025']-stats['cumulative_2024']:,}-satellite net increase in a single year.</li>
      <li><strong>2026 (partial):</strong> The first three months of 2026 have already added {stats['total']-stats['cumulative_2025']:,} active entries, suggesting the pace is not slowing.</li>
    </ul>

