    <p>The bimodal distribution of mean motion reflects the physical separation between LEO, MEO, and GEO. The sharp peak above 14 rev/day corresponds to the Starlink and OneWeb shells, while the smaller peaks near 1 rev/day and ~2 rev/day mark GEO and GNSS orbits respectively.</p>
